# Build context of the project image (Dockerfile, P3-2): an allow-list.
# Everything is excluded, then only what the image needs is let back in. Never in
# the context: .env and every secret, the local lake (lake/), the SQLite metadata
# DB (airflow.db*), airflow.cfg, logs, the local virtualenvs (.venv,
# transform/.venv), source data (data/), lineage events, the DuckDB warehouse.
# tests/unit/test_p3_2_image.py checks these rules, and
# tests/integration/test_p3_2_image_context.py the real build context (Docker).
*

!Dockerfile
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!dags/
!pipeline/
!utils/
!storage/
!config/
!examples/config/
!transform/
!deploy/airflow/pools.json
!deploy/k8s/image/

# Generated or local files inside the allowed directories.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.env
**/.env.*
transform/.venv/
transform/target/
transform/logs/
transform/dbt_packages/
transform/*.duckdb
transform/*.duckdb.wal
transform/.user.yml
utils/script_shell/
# Secrets or local state that could end up in an allowed directory (SEC-8).
**/airflow.cfg
**/*.generated
**/*.db
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*credentials*
**/.user.yml
